WEBVTT

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.610
Let's try climbing to the high
ground in the middle of the island.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:08.290
There might be land nearby,

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:09.940
and I'd like to see the shape
of the whole island.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.700
<b>Oasis Found?!</b>

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.600
We made it!

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.580
I don't see anything.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.570
So we really are in the middle of the ocean...

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:25.460
It seems so.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:29.770
That's...

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:30.670
What?

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.000
Hey! Is someone there?

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.040
Hey! Is someone there?

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.360
There doesn't seem to be any response...

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.050
Let's go check it out!

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:43.890
Yes.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.520
Right. Let's go.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:50.950
There's no one here.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.150
This should be the right area.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:54.610
Oh! There!

00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:59.020
Smoke?

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.940
Isn't it steam?

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:04.370
So it wasn't a signal fire?

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:05.460
It's hot!

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.630
This water has to be over 100 degrees.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:10.750
Then, that means this is...

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.500
A hot spring?

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:17.030
It's a lot saltier than seawater.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:19.600
It must be bubbling up
under here and collecting.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.010
Huh?

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:22.670
These rocks...

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:25.500
Doesn't it look like they've
been arranged by someone?

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.260
Maybe someone was going to
use it as an onsen!

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:30.290
You're right.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.230
We don't know when it's from,

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:34.650
but probably around the same
time as the abandoned house. Or—

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.610
Hey! We don't need analysis right now, do we?

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:40.240
There's only one thing for us to do, right?

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:41.570
That's right, Homare-san!

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:43.290
There's only one thing to do!

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:44.610
Huh?

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:55.710
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:58.510
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.080
This is amazing!

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:09.080
I never would have thought I'd
be able to have a bath on this island!

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.300
We've been doing nothing
but walking since yesterday...

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.560
I can feel it soaking into my whole body...

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.660
We've discovered all kinds of things.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:20.420
Oh! Right! Let's use those!

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:21.760
Oh, those!

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.890
Oh! It's a yuzu bath!

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:32.100
It feels like a resort...

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.090
What a lovely fragrance...

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:35.980
I'm sure it'll do wonders for our complexions.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.260
Yes.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:41.070
Citrus fruit peels contain
a component called limonene.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:45.120
It can help improve the immune
system and moisturize skin, but...

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.670
We'd collected these for food...

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.890
Why not? Every once in a while...

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.620
Stop it!

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:58.030
<i>I-I guess it's not far to where
we camped yesterday.</i>

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.350
I said cut it out!

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:00.130
<i>We can relax here for a while.</i>

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:05.680
The moon is beautiful...

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:08.370
It's a waxing moon tonight.

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:12.560
The line dividing the halves
of the moon point roughly south.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.440
At least, in the Northern Hemisphere.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:17.360
<b>South</b>

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:17.360
We could be in the Southern
Hemisphere, you know?

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.500
I can see the North Star over there,

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.190
so we're in the Northern Hemisphere.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:25.770
You can find the North Star using
Cassiopeia and the Big Dipper.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.820
Do you like stars, Homare-san?

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.580
I love them, too!

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:33.330
Uh... I... It's not that
I particularly like them...

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:36.740
The North Star is approximately
430 light years from Earth.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:39.570
It's in Ursa Minor, also called "the little bear,"
and is often referred to as Polaris.

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:40.840
Polaris A is a yellow super giant,

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:44.940
a Cepheid variable type,
 and it orbits around Polaris B,

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.550
Hey. Does the water seem cooler?

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.820
which is a main sequence star, 
making them binary stars.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.220
This is—

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.680
The seawater is getting in here!

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:53.840
Polaris Ab is a dwarf star
and companion to Polaris A,

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.310
What? Oh, it's starting to go down...

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:55.310
and the three stars together
make it a triple star system!

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:56.220
Did you know that

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:57.320
Wh-What?

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:58.710
the primary star, Polaris Aa, 
is approximately 30 times the size of our sun?

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.070
And Polaris A and Polaris B—

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:09.600
Hey! Is everyone all right?

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:14.120
I see.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:17.150
At high tide, it sinks under the ocean.

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:20.000
That really scared me!

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.630
It was a little bit of a disaster,
but we discovered a lot of things.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:25.650
Huh?

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:26.760
Well...

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:31.680
There might not be anyone here now,
but someone did live here once!

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.850
Yeah. You're right.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:35.730
Yes.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.130
Next time, let's explore deeper into the island!

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:45.190
Yes. We might find something.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:49.350
True. We might find something even better.

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:51.650
Yes...

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.140
I hope you find something...

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:55.120
Well, shall we head back?

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.970
If this wasn't all rock, we could live here...

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:00.220
We'll come back to use the onsen again.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.510
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.250
Yeah?

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:07.340
Shion-san! Asuka-san!

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.720
Time to wake up.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.460
Time for breakfast.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:12.390
Meat?

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:13.990
There's no meat...

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:16.270
Once we've finished eating,
let's head back to the shelter.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:19.940
But before that, there's
somewhere I'd like to go.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.110
I found it yesterday,
and I keep wondering about it.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:26.030
Yes.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:27.460
Homare-san?

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:29.910
Yes. I think we can use that.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:33.180
It's 8-ply rope used for anchoring boats.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.130
I'd like to acquire it if possible.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:38.790
Would a rope that thick be useful?

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:42.270
If we unply it, it will be thinner,
and we can make it longer, too.

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:44.710
We might be able to rebuild our shelter.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:48.100
But how will we get it? If we fall...

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:49.630
It's pretty far down.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:53.510
There's about 10 meters from the top
of this cliff to the surface of the water.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.860
The vine attached to this
weight is about 5 meters long.

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:59.980
If the water isn't at least that
deep, it would be dangerous.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.650
The water? Dangerous?

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:05.200
If the vine submerges
completely, we know it's safe.

00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:06.820
Okay.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:07.790
Huh?

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:09.860
Homare!

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:13.510
She's crazy!

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:14.410
She definitely is.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:20.720
Are you all right?

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:24.440
How is she going to climb back up?

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.480
That's gotta be impossible, right?

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.010
Right. I think it'll work.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:38.630
There's a move used for climbing
narrow spaces like this called "chimney."

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:39.520
Okay!

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:45.770
<i>Turn sideways and climb by pressing
your back and feet away from each other.</i>

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:52.750
Sh-She's really amazing...

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:54.620
She's like a lady gorilla...

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:57.490
She's going to hear you!

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.760
I can hear you.

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.540
You did it, Homare!

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.280
Rain?

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:08.270
This isn't good.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.860
It's falling harder.

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:12.470
Hurry to the shelter.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:23.730
In preparation for rain, we made
the roof on the thick side, but...

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.870
when it rains this much,
it doesn't do much good.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:31.320
The fire went out so we can't
dry our clothes either...

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.110
All we can do is wait here.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:35.660
Should we play a word game?

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.120
This is stupid!

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:41.910
I'm already soaked! I'll go get
something from the ocean.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.390
Hey, Asuka! Don't!

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:47.670
It'll be fine!

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:48.950
Huh?

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:49.840
What was that?

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:59.560
<i>Sh-She's dead!</i>

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:04.740
She got an electric shock.
From the lightning strike.

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:07.350
If it had been within 30 meters of us,
that would have been bad.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:13.150
M-My head... that really hurt...

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:22.370
Say, it's really scary.
Couldn't we go into the forest?

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:23.920
Well...

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:27.970
If lightning struck a tree, the forest
would be more dangerous than here.

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:30.740
Though it is possible it will strike here—

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:32.040
No!

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:33.170
There is one thing we can do.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.380
If you want protection from lightning,

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:38.550
you can find something to serve as a 
lightning rod, and stay 4 meters away.

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:42.260
If you're inside a 45 degree angle,
they say you'll be fairly safe.

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:47.560
We don't have a lightning rod, and
there aren't any tall trees around here!

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:50.790
Then, why don't we make something?

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:52.650
We could use driftwood.

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:55.240
That's true. Should we try it?

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:58.450
There we go.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:04.790
Okay. That should do it.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.250
Homare! How far is 4 meters?

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.670
How do we measure 45 degrees?

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:12.590
My stride is 62 cm, so...

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:15.370
This should be about 4.5 meters.

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.510
Stop it! You're heavy!

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:31.520
Looks like the rain's stopped.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:36.190
Hey! It's cleared up, so let's
all go get something in the ocean!

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:38.850
After what just happened, she still...

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:41.160
That is the face of someone who doesn't learn.

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:45.510
Asuka-san! Getting too excited
out there is dangerous—

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:53.370
<i>Sh-She's dead?!</i>

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:58.040
It might have cleared,
but you can't let your guard down.

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:01.830
In the ocean, there are things
like jimble jellyfish...

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:04.220
in other words, electric jellyfish.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:10.540
Fresh water could cause
pH shock, so I'll use seawater.

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:13.980
I don't understand everything,
but thanks Homare.

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:16.060
It really hurt...

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:17.570
All right, all right...

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:18.870
Is it swelling?

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:19.930
Just a little.

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:21.250
Homare-san has it rough, too...

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:22.030
Will it leave a scar?

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:23.530
The two of us should act responsibly.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:24.330
Huh?

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:29.130
Next time, Case 9:
 "Homare's Papa."

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:30.860
<b>Homare's Papa</b>
